## Phase 1 — Layout-Aware Chunking + Contextual Headers
**Why:** The current `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(1000, 0)` in [retriever.py L47](file:///c:/Users/deepa/OneDrive/Desktop/projects/Contract_Checker-main/Contract_Checker-main/retriever.py#L47) slices text blindly, loses headings, and the 4-page split in [app.py L91-93](file:///c:/Users/deepa/OneDrive/Desktop/projects/Contract_Checker-main/Contract_Checker-main/app.py#L91-L93) can cut clauses in half.

### Task 1.1: Add `pymupdf4llm` for PDF → Structured Markdown
- **New dependency:** `pip install pymupdf4llm`
- **New module:** `document_parser.py`
- **What it does:**
  1. Convert PDF to Markdown preserving `#`, `##`, `###` headings and tables
  2. Inject `[Page X]` markers at actual page boundaries
  3. Split by Markdown heading boundaries (not character count)
  4. Each chunk gets a breadcrumb header prepended:
     `[Doc: Nexify Policy | Section 2: Payment Terms | Clause 2.1 | Page 3]`

### Task 1.2: Build Parent-Child chunk index
- **Inside `document_parser.py`:**
  - **Child chunks:** Individual sub-clauses (2.1, 2.2) — small, sharp vectors for search
  - **Parent chunks:** Full sections (Section 2) — complete context for LLM reasoning
  - Each child stores a `parent_id` pointer
  - When child matches → return parent text to compliance checker

### Task 1.3: Replace clause extraction approach
- **Current:** [app.py L91-104](file:///c:/Users/deepa/OneDrive/Desktop/projects/Contract_Checker-main/Contract_Checker-main/app.py#L91-L104) splits into 4-page chunks, each sent to `Extract_clause.py` for LLM extraction
- **New:** `document_parser.py` splits the vendor contract deterministically by clause headings (0 LLM calls for this step)
- **Fallback:** If the PDF has no clear headings (scanned/flat), THEN use LLM extraction on the full Markdown text
- **Update:** [Extract_clause.py](file:///c:/Users/deepa/OneDrive/Desktop/projects/Contract_Checker-main/Contract_Checker-main/Extract_clause.py) becomes a fallback, not the primary path

### Task 1.4: Update retriever to use contextual chunks
- **Modify:** [retriever.py](file:///c:/Users/deepa/OneDrive/Desktop/projects/Contract_Checker-main/Contract_Checker-main/retriever.py) `process_uploaded_files()`
- **Replace:** `RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter(chunk_size=1000, chunk_overlap=0)` with the new `document_parser.py` chunking
- **Store:** Both child chunks (for search) and parent chunks (for LLM context) in the retriever

**Acceptance criteria for Phase 1:**
- [ ] PDFs converted to Markdown with headings preserved
- [ ] Every chunk has a breadcrumb header (visible in retrieved docs)
- [ ] Parent-child relationship established
- [ ] No clause is split across page boundaries
- [ ] Retriever uses contextual chunks, not naive 1000-char splits

